{%- comment -%}
  Resolve the collection behind this row once, up here, because both the
  summary and the View All rung inside the panel want the count, and the
  knit thumbnails want the product list.

  A menu item only carries link.object when it was built in the admin by
  picking the collection; an item typed or pasted as a URL is type 'http'
  with nothing attached. So fall back to the handle in the URL.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign panel_collection = nil
  if link.type == 'collection_link'
    assign panel_collection = link.object
  elsif link.url contains '/collections/'
    assign panel_handle = link.url | split: '/collections/' | last | split: '?' | first | split: '/' | first
    assign panel_collection = collections[panel_handle]
  endif

  assign panel_count = 0
  if panel_collection.handle != blank
    assign panel_count = panel_collection.all_products_count
  endif
-%}

<details is="menu-details">
  <summary class="drawer__menu-item block heading text-2xl leading-none tracking-tight cursor-pointer relative" aria-expanded="false">
    <span class="onrepeat-nav__label">{{ link.title | escape }}</span>
    {%- if panel_count > 0 -%}<span class="onrepeat-nav__count">{{ panel_count }}</span>{%- endif -%}
  </summary>
  <div class="drawer__submenu z-1 absolute top-0 left-0 flex flex-col w-full h-full" data-parent>
    {%- comment -%}
      The panel header doubles as the way back. The theme shipped it as a bare
      title with no affordance at all — the chevron is what says "this closes".

      The Devanagari beside it is set per handle rather than derived: there is
      no transliteration filter in Liquid, and a wrong one is worse than none,
      so anything unlisted simply renders without it.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign panel_deva = ''
      case panel_collection.handle
        when 'polo'
          assign panel_deva = 'पोलो'
        when 't-shirts'
          assign panel_deva = 'टी-शर्ट'
      endcase
    -%}
    <button type="button" class="onrepeat-nav__back tracking-tight heading text-base shrink-0 flex items-center gap-3 w-full" data-close>
      {%- render 'icon', icon: 'chevron-left', size: 'xs' -%}
      <em>{{ link.title | escape }}</em>
      {%- if panel_deva != blank -%}<i class="onrepeat-nav__deva">{{ panel_deva }}</i>{%- endif -%}
    </button>
    <ul class="drawer__scrollable flex flex-col h-full">
      {%- comment -%}
        There is otherwise no way out of a panel to the thing it is about: the
        header above is a close button, not a link, so a shopper who opens
        "Polo" can reach eight knit families but never the 48 polos themselves.
        This is that missing rung.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <li>
        <a class="drawer__menu-item onrepeat-nav__viewall block leading-none" href="{{ link.url }}">
          <span class="onrepeat-nav__label">{{ 'sections.featured_collection.view_all' | t }} {{ link.title | escape }}</span>
          {%- if panel_count > 0 -%}<span class="onrepeat-nav__count">{{ panel_count }} pieces</span>{%- endif -%}
        </a>
      </li>

      {%- comment -%}
        Knit-family thumbnails. CANE, CORD, HIVE and VANE are the design
        language of the range but they are unreadable as words — nobody can
        picture a knit called HIVE. The image is found by matching the child
        link's title against the first word of a product title in the parent
        collection, so it needs no uploaded assets and no per-family setting:
        the photography is already in the catalogue. Falls back to a plain row
        when the parent is not a collection or nothing matches.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign family_source = panel_collection -%}

      {%- for childlink in link.links -%}
        <li>
          {%- if childlink.links != blank -%}
            <details is="menu-details">
              <summary class="drawer__menu-item block heading text-2xl leading-none tracking-tight cursor-pointer relative" aria-expanded="false">
                {{- childlink.title | escape -}}
              </summary>
              <div class="drawer__submenu z-1 absolute top-0 left-0 w-full h-full">
                <button type="button" class="tracking-tight heading text-base flex items-center gap-3 w-full" data-close>{{ childlink.title | escape }}</button>
                <ul class="drawer__scrollable flex flex-col h-full">
                  {%- for grandchildlink in childlink.links -%}
                    <li>
                      <a class="drawer__menu-item block heading text-2xl leading-none tracking-tight" href="{{ grandchildlink.url }}">{{ grandchildlink.title | escape }}</a>
                    </li>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                </ul>
              </div>
            </details>
          {%- else -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign family_image = blank
              assign family_count = 0
              if family_source.handle != blank
                assign family_key = childlink.title | downcase | strip
                comment
                  One pass per family, counting as it goes rather than
                  breaking on the first hit — the count is the second half of
                  the row and it has to be the real number, not an estimate.
                  Liquid caps a bare for at 50 items, which is why the whole
                  block is gated on a collection that fits inside that.
                endcomment
                for family_product in family_source.products limit: 50
                  assign product_first_word = family_product.title | split: ' ' | first | downcase | strip
                  if product_first_word == family_key
                    assign family_count = family_count | plus: 1
                    if family_image == blank
                      comment
                        preview_image, not the media itself: several of these
                        products lead with a video, and image_url has nothing
                        to work with on a video object. preview_image is on
                        both media types, so the thumbnail renders either way.
                      endcomment
                      assign family_image = family_product.featured_media.preview_image
                    endif
                  endif
                endfor
              endif
            -%}
            {%- if family_image != blank -%}
              <a class="drawer__menu-item onrepeat-nav__family block leading-none" href="{{ childlink.url }}">
                <span class="onrepeat-nav__thumb">
                  {{- family_image | image_url: width: 132 | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', widths: '44,88,132', alt: childlink.title -}}
                </span>
                <span class="onrepeat-nav__label">{{ childlink.title | escape }}</span>
                {%- if family_count > 0 -%}<span class="onrepeat-nav__count">{{ family_count }}</span>{%- endif -%}
              </a>
            {%- else -%}
              <a class="drawer__menu-item block heading text-2xl leading-none tracking-tight" href="{{ childlink.url }}">{{ childlink.title | escape }}</a>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        </li>
      {%- endfor -%}

      {%- if enable_mega_menu -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign show_promotions = false
          if block.settings.promo_image_1 != blank or block.settings.promo_image_2 != blank or block.settings.promo_image_3 != blank or block.settings.promo_image_4 != blank or block.settings.promo_image_5 != blank or block.settings.promo_image_6 != blank
            assign show_promotions = true
          endif
        -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if show_promotions -%}
        <li class="drawer__promotions">
          <ul class="mega-menu__list grid grid-cols-2 w-full h-full" role="list" tabindex="-1">
            {%- for i in (1..6) -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign promo_image = 'promo_image_' | append: i
                assign promo_image = block.settings[promo_image]
              -%}
              {%- if promo_image != blank -%}
                {%- liquid
                  assign promo_image_ratio = 'promo_image_ratio_' | append: i
                  assign promo_image_ratio = block.settings[promo_image_ratio]
    
                  assign promo_heading = 'promo_heading_' | append: i
                  assign promo_heading = block.settings[promo_heading]
    
                  assign promo_subtext = 'promo_subtext_' | append: i
                  assign promo_subtext = block.settings[promo_subtext]
    
                  assign promo_overlay_content = 'promo_overlay_content_' | append: i
                  assign promo_overlay_content = block.settings[promo_overlay_content]
    
                  assign promo_link = 'promo_link_' | append: i
                  assign promo_link = block.settings[promo_link]
  
                  assign promo_tag = 'promo_tag_' | append: i
                  assign promo_tag = block.settings[promo_tag]
    
                  assign promo_color_text = 'promo_color_text_' | append: i
                  assign promo_color_text = block.settings[promo_color_text]
    
                  assign promo_color_overlay = 'promo_color_overlay_' | append: i
                  assign promo_color_overlay = block.settings[promo_color_overlay]
    
                  assign promo_overlay_opacity = 'promo_overlay_opacity_' | append: i
                  assign promo_overlay_opacity = block.settings[promo_overlay_opacity]
                -%}
                <li class="mega-menu__item flex opacity-0 w-full">
                  <div class="media-card media-card--{{ settings.card_style }}{% if promo_overlay_content %} media-card--overlap{% endif %} overflow-hidden">
                    <a class="media-card__link flex flex-col w-full h-full relative"{% if promo_link != blank %} href="{{ promo_link }}"{% else %} role="link" aria-disabled="true"{% endif %}
                      aria-label="{{ promo_heading | default: promo_subtext | escape }}"
                      style="--color-foreground: {{ promo_color_text.rgb }}; --color-overlay: {{ promo_color_overlay.rgb }}; --overlay-opacity: {{ promo_overlay_opacity | divided_by: 100.0 }};"
                    >
                      {%- if promo_tag != blank -%}
                        <div class="badges z-2 absolute grid gap-3 pointer-events-none">
                          <span class="badge badge--onsale flex items-center gap-1d5 font-medium leading-none rounded-full">{{ promo_tag | escape }}</span>
                        </div>
                      {%- endif -%}
                      <div class="media media--{{ promo_image_ratio }} relative overflow-hidden">
                        {{- promo_image | image_url: width: promo_image.width | image_tag: loading: 'lazy', widths: '180,360,540,720,900,1080', is: 'lazy-image' -}}
                      </div>
                      {%- if promo_heading != blank or promo_subtext != blank -%}
                        <div class="media-card__content flex justify-between items-center gap-4 w-full">
                          <div class="media-card__text opacity-0 shrink-1 grid gap-0d5">
                            {%- if promo_heading != blank -%}
                              <p>
                                <span class="heading reversed-link text-lg tracking-tighter leading-tight">{{ promo_heading | escape }}</span>
                              </p>
                            {%- endif -%}
                            {%- if promo_subtext != blank -%}
                              <p class="leading-none text-xs xl:text-sm hidden md:block">{{ promo_subtext }}</p>
                            {%- endif -%}
                          </div>
                          {%- render 'icon', icon: 'arrow-right', size: 'xs', class: 'transform shrink-0 hidden md:block' -%}
                        </div>
                      {%- endif -%}
                    </a>
                  </div>
                </li>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ul>
        </li>
        {%- comment -%}
          The mega menu block has carried a button label and link since the
          theme shipped; the desktop menu renders it and the drawer never did,
          so the panel ended on a grid of cards with no way forward.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- if block.settings.button_label != blank and block.settings.button_link != blank -%}
          <li>
            <a class="onrepeat-nav__cta flex items-center justify-center" href="{{ block.settings.button_link }}">
              {{- block.settings.button_label | escape -}}
            </a>
          </li>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    </ul>
  </div>
</details>
